  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Alice is given two arrays AAA and BBB, each consisting of NNN integers. Note that both arrays have **1-based indexing**.\n\nShe can perform the following operation on array AAA any number of times:\n\n\nChoose any 2≤i≤N−22 \\leq i \\leq N-22≤i≤N−2 and update the values of Ai−1,Ai,Ai+1,Ai+2A_{i-1} , A_{i} , A_{i+1} , A_{i+2}Ai−1​,Ai​,Ai+1​,Ai+2​ as following :\n\nAi−1A_{i-1}Ai−1​ = Ai−1+Ai+Ai+1A_{i-1} + A_{i} + A_{i+1}Ai−1​+Ai​+Ai+1​\nAiA_{i}Ai​ = −Ai+1-A_{i+1}−Ai+1​\nAi+1A_{i+1}Ai+1​ = −Ai-A_{i}−Ai​\nAi+2A_{i+2}Ai+2​ = Ai+2+Ai+1+AiA_{i+2} + A_{i+1} + A_{i}Ai+2​+Ai+1​+Ai​\n\n\nNote: The new values of Ai−1,Ai,Ai+1,Ai+2A_{i-1} , A_{i} , A_{i+1} , A_{i+2}Ai−1​,Ai​,Ai+1​,Ai+2​ are updated simultaneously using the old values.\n\nFind whether it is possible to transform the array AAA to BBB using any number of operations.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a integer NNN — the length of the arrays.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers - values of the array AAA .\nThe third line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers - values of the array BBB .\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print `Yes` if it is possible to transform array AAA into array BBB using any number of operations, otherwise print `No`.\n\n\nYou may print each character of the string in uppercase or lowercase (for example, the strings `YES`, `yEs`, `yes`, and `yeS` will all be treated as identical).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "4≤N≤2⋅1054 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^54≤N≤2⋅105",
      "−109≤Ai,Bi≤109-10^9 \\leq A_i , B_i \\leq 10^9−109≤Ai​,Bi​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
